  <section id="episode1" class="sticker-zone">
    <img class="sticker" style="top:36px; right:-14px; transform: rotate(8deg);" src="data:image/png;base64," alt="">
    <div class="section-head">
      <div class="filecode">EPISODE 01 — VOLLEYBALL AT ITS FINEST</div>
      <h2>Eclipse Horizon vs. Freerow</h2>
      <p class="section-desc">Pre-match press, filed before either team took the court.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="video-slot">
      <iframe src="https://www.youtube.com/embed/a7fFOOy28WA" title="ZOTV Episode 1 — Volleyball at Its Finest" allow="accelerometer; autoplay; clipboard-write; encrypted-media; gyroscope; picture-in-picture" allowfullscreen loading="lazy"></iframe>
    </div>

    <div class="transcript">
      <div class="transcript-head">
        <h3>Natsukawa Tokihara</h3>
        <span>ECLIPSE HORIZON</span>
      </div>
      <div class="qa">
        <div class="q">Eclipse Horizon comes into tonight on a strong run. How are you feeling heading into this one?</div>
        <div class="a">Good. Focused. We've prepared for this matchup specifically — Freerow isn't a team you can go in on autopilot against.</div>
      </div>
      <div class="qa">
        <div class="q">Freerow's biggest threat is their wing spiker, Sagita. You two have a history that goes back before either of you turned pro. What's it like preparing to play against him?</div>
        <div class="a">He's the reason I picked up a volleyball in the first place. So there's a version of tonight that's just two guys who grew up on the same court, and there's a version that's two professionals trying to win a match. I'm trying to stay in the second version for as long as I can.</div>
      </div>
      <div class="qa">
        <div class="q">Analysts have flagged his left-side approach as one of the hardest to read in the division. Does knowing him personally give you an edge there?</div>
        <div class="a">Maybe on paper. He also knows exactly how I read a swing, which cancels most of that out. It'll come down to who adjusts faster in the moment, not who knows who.</div>
      </div>
      <div class="qa">
        <div class="q">Eclipse Horizon's coaching staff has called this a measuring-stick match heading into the back half of the season. Do you feel that pressure?</div>
        <div class="a">I'd rather call it an opportunity. Every match is a measuring stick if you treat it that way. I don't think about it much beyond that.</div>
      </div>
      <div class="qa">
        <div class="q">Last one — you wear a scarf under your uniform every match, including tonight. Can you tell us anything about that?</div>
        <div class="a aside">He smiles slightly and declines to answer.</div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="transcript">
      <div class="transcript-head">
        <h3>Sagita</h3>
        <span>FREEROW — WING SPIKER</span>
      </div>
      <div class="qa">
        <div class="q">Freerow is the underdog on paper tonight. How do you approach a match like this?</div>
        <div class="a">Same as any other. I'm not really an underdog-versus-favorite kind of player. I just want to go out there and play good volleyball.</div>
      </div>
      <div class="qa">
        <div class="q">You're facing Natsukawa Tokihara tonight, someone you've known since before either of you went pro. What's that matchup mean to you?</div>
        <div class="a">It means a lot, honestly. He's one of my closest friends. Getting to share a court with him as opponents instead of teammates — that's rare, and I don't take it for granted.</div>
      </div>
      <div class="qa">
        <div class="q">Some players in your position would be feeling real pressure. This is being called a measuring-stick game for Eclipse Horizon. Does that pressure transfer to you?</div>
        <div class="a">Not really. I don't play to prove something to a standings table. I play because I love this game, and I love playing it against people who push me. If winning tonight means I had to stop enjoying myself to get there, I'd rather lose.</div>
      </div>
      <div class="qa">
        <div class="q">That's an unusual thing to hear from a competitor at this level.</div>
        <div class="a">Maybe. But I didn't get into volleyball to win trophies. I got into it because of how it felt the first time I hit a ball clean. I still chase that feeling more than I chase the scoreboard.</div>
      </div>
      <div class="qa">
        <div class="q">So what does a win look like for you tonight, if not the scoreboard?</div>
        <div class="a">Both of us playing our best and walking off still smiling at each other. Everything else is extra.</div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="conceptart">
    <div class="section-head">
      <div class="filecode">01 — EARLY VISUAL DEVELOPMENT</div>
      <h2>Concept art</h2>
      <p class="section-desc">Designs and drafts from before anything was final.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="art-grid">
      <div class="art-piece wide">
        <div class="art-slot wide filled"><img src="data:image/jpeg;base64," alt="Early sketch sheet of Junia, Shade and Natsu"></div>
        <div class="art-comment">Everything started in Voidless, our small community — three of its leaders each had their own volleyball/Spike OC. The idea began as a skin pack for those three characters, then grew into "what if each skin got its own special-episode story?" That question is what eventually became ZOTV.</div>
      </div>
      <div class="art-piece">
        <div class="art-slot filled"><img src="data:image/jpeg;base64," alt="Natsukawa Tokihara concept sheet"></div>
        <div class="art-comment">Natsukawa Tokihara — Eclipse Horizon, Wing Spiker. 6'3" (192cm), 216 lbs (98kg), born August 2. Stat hexagon: Power 5, Jumping 4, Stamina 4, Intelligence 5, Technique 4, Speed 4.</div>
      </div>
      <div class="art-piece">
        <div class="art-slot filled"><img src="data:image/jpeg;base64," alt="Sagita concept sheet"></div>
        <div class="art-comment">Sagita — Freerow, Wing Spiker. 6'4" (196cm), 222 lbs (101kg). Stat hexagon: Power 5, Jumping 5, Stamina 3, Intelligence 4, Technique 4, Speed 4.</div>
      </div>
      <div class="art-piece">
        <div class="art-slot filled"><img src="data:image/jpeg;base64," alt="Nebel Dorn player file and character sheet"></div>
        <div class="art-comment">Nebel Dorn's in-universe player file — Middle Blocker, 210cm, left-handed, formerly of VWL's Red Lions, status marked suspended, rated Tier SSS.</div>
      </div>
      <div class="art-piece">
        <div class="art-slot filled"><img src="data:image/jpeg;base64," alt="Episode 1 storyboard thumbnails"></div>
        <div class="art-comment">Rough shot-by-shot storyboard panels for Episode 1, blocking out camera angles and pacing before any animation began.</div>
      </div>
      <div class="art-piece">
        <div class="art-slot filled"><img src="data:image/jpeg;base64," alt="Early environment concept art"></div>
        <div class="art-comment">An early environment mood piece exploring the show's cosmic, void-lit visual language.</div>
      </div>
      <div class="art-piece wide">
        <div class="art-slot wide filled"><img src="data:image/jpeg;base64," alt="Additional team and court concept designs"></div>
        <div class="art-comment">Additional uniform designs for another league team, alongside early sketches of a men's volleyball court and a suspended player's locker door.</div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="facts" class="sticker-zone">
    <img class="sticker" style="top:2px; right:-16px; transform: rotate(10deg);" src="data:image/png;base64," alt="">
    <div class="section-head">
      <div class="filecode">02 — LOOSE ENDS</div>
      <h2>Fun facts</h2>
    </div>

    <div class="facts">
      <div class="fact"><p><strong>Voice before vision.</strong> Every line of dialogue, the score, and the sound effects were finished before a single frame of Episode 1 was animated.</p></div>
      <div class="fact"><p><strong>One tool, start to finish.</strong> Everything in the episode was animated in ToonSquid.</p></div>
      <div class="fact"><p><strong>The rivalry outlived high school.</strong> Natsukawa and Sagita's friendship never ended — once both turned pro, they ended up facing each other in plenty of league matches.</p></div>
      <div class="fact"><p><strong>Nebel has a real-world blueprint.</strong> He's based on Tobias Krick, middle blocker for the German national volleyball team — right down to matching his 210cm height.</p></div>
      <div class="fact"><p><strong>The name is a nod.</strong> Zenith of the Void takes its title, and part of its DNA, from the mobile game The Spike Cross.</p></div>
    </div>
  </section>

